<h1>SecureU — Step-by-Step Setup & Execution Guide</h1>
<p><strong>Course:</strong> Java Programming / DBMS Lab &bull; <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> 100% Pure Java Swing (JFrame) + MySQL JDBC</p>

<h2>1. System Prerequisites</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Component</th>
      <th>Required Version</th>
      <th>System Location</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Java JDK</strong></td>
      <td>JDK 17, 21, or 27</td>
      <td><code>C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-27.0.1.0.3\bin\java.exe</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>MySQL Server</strong></td>
      <td>XAMPP MySQL or MySQL 8.x</td>
      <td>Port 3306 (<code>http://localhost/phpmyadmin</code>)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. MySQL Database Setup (XAMPP)</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Start MySQL:</strong> Open XAMPP Control Panel and click <strong>"Start"</strong> next to MySQL (port 3306).</li>
  <li><strong>Open phpMyAdmin:</strong> Go to <code>http://localhost/phpmyadmin</code> in your web browser.</li>
  <li><strong>Create Database:</strong> Click the <em>"Databases"</em> tab, enter database name <code>CollegeComplaint</code>, and click <em>"Create"</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Import SQL File:</strong> Select <code>CollegeComplaint</code> from the left menu &rarr; click the <em>"Import"</em> tab &rarr; choose <code>sql/CollegeComplaint.sql</code> &rarr; click <strong>"Import"</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<div class="tip">
  <strong>Note:</strong> Java also features an automatic database seeder. If the database is newly created, it seeds 50+ sample complaints automatically on startup!
</div>

<h2>3. Running as Pure Java Desktop Application (GUI Mode)</h2>
<p>This mode opens a 100% native Java desktop application (<code>JFrame</code>) with no browser involved.</p>

<h3>Method 1: One-Click Desktop Launcher (Recommended)</h3>
<p>In your project folder, double-click: <strong><code>Launch-CollegeComplaint.bat</code></strong> (or <code>run-desktop-java.bat</code>).</p>

<h3>Method 2: From PowerShell</h3>
<pre>
cd "C:\Users\Hariprasad\Videos\JAVA PROJECT"
.\run.ps1
</pre>

<h3>Method 3: Direct Java Command</h3>
<pre>
& "C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-27.0.1.0.3\bin\java.exe" -jar CollegeComplaint.jar
</pre>

<h2>4. Running in Terminal Console Mode (CLI / Viva Mode)</h2>
<p>Use this mode when your teacher or lab examiner asks: <em>"Show me the Java console output in the terminal itself!"</em></p>

<h3>Method 1: One-Click Terminal Launcher</h3>
<p>In your project folder, double-click: <strong><code>Launch-Terminal-Console.bat</code></strong>.</p>

<h3>Method 2: From PowerShell / Command Prompt</h3>
<pre>
cd "C:\Users\Hariprasad\Videos\JAVA PROJECT"
.\run.ps1 --terminal
</pre>

<h3>Terminal Commands Available for Demonstration:</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width:15%">Command</th>
      <th style="width:35%">Action</th>
      <th style="width:50%">What is Displayed in Terminal</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1</strong></td>
      <td>View All Complaints Table</td>
      <td>Formatted ASCII table of 50+ complaints with ID, Student, Department, Category, Status, and Date.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2</strong></td>
      <td>Filter by Status</td>
      <td>Prompt accepts <code>P</code> (Pending), <code>I</code> (In Progress), or <code>R</code> (Resolved) and filters records via SQL query.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3</strong></td>
      <td>View Registered Students</td>
      <td>ASCII table of registered students with ID, Name, Department, Email, and Phone number.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4</strong></td>
      <td>Submit Complaint via Terminal</td>
      <td>Interactive input prompts for Student ID, Category, and Description. Executes SQL <code>INSERT</code> via <code>PreparedStatement</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>5</strong></td>
      <td>Update Status via Terminal</td>
      <td>Prompts for Complaint ID, new status, and remarks. Executes SQL <code>UPDATE</code> in MySQL.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>6</strong></td>
      <td>Database Metrics Overview</td>
      <td>Prints live SQL <code>COUNT(*)</code> summary calculations.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>7</strong></td>
      <td>Open Pure Java Swing Window</td>
      <td>Launches the desktop GUI window directly from the console.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

